{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:AppendixKnotPeriodicTable.RecursiveAtomKnotAtlas","@type":"LeanModule","name":"AppendixKnotPeriodicTable.RecursiveAtomKnotAtlas","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.filtration_certificate_format_specified","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.filtration_certificate_format_specified","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L227-L233","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FiltrationCertificateFormat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FiltrationCertificateFormat","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L210-L225","doc":"Filtration certificate format produced by gb_filtration_jet_tracker.py:\na Hecke element E ∈ H_n(q) is recorded as a map\n    FiltrationCertificate := ℕ → List (Perm n × ℚ(q))\nwhere FiltrationCertificate grade lists every basis element T_w with\nCoxeter length ℓ(w) = grade and its symbolic-q coefficient.\n\nThe jet-order log is the ordered list of reduction events; each\nevent tags the multiplication step T_w · T_i with (ℓ(w), ℓ(ws_i),\nrelation ∈ {ascending, hecke-quadratic}).\n\nConcrete predicate: every atlas entry has a non-empty\n`braid_word` field (the certificate carries the σ-generator\nsequence).  Closes by `decide` on the proton + neutron seed\nentries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.principled_path_for_atom_knot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.principled_path_for_atom_knot","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L203-L208","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PrincipledPathForAtomKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PrincipledPathForAtomKnot","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L181-L201","doc":"The principled path for any new atom-knot identification: a JOINT\nSDP on the full mass tower (over all confinement levels ℓ and all\natoms simultaneously), with Gröbner-Shirshov filtration tracking\nand jet-order tracking, yielding canonical T_w ∈ H_{n_0}(q_0)\nPER ATOM as a structured certificate.\n\nThe Markov closure of T_w is then taken in S^3, and Vol_hyp is\ncomputed at ≥ 50 decimal digits via\n`hp_volume_of_link_closure(braid_word, digits=50)` for comparison\nto AME via B_pred = ρ · m_e · Vol_hyp.\n\nPer-atom volume-match search is FORBIDDEN as a derivation route:\nthe SDP must be joint over the tower so the GB filtration and the\njet ordering are consistent across confinement levels.\n\nConcrete predicate: `principledAtlas atomKnotAtlas = atomKnotAtlas`\n— every atlas entry has a methodology other than\n`deprecatedVolumeMatch`.  The proton + neutron seed entries both\nuse `principledDerivation`, so this closes by `decide`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.atlas_witness_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.atlas_witness_derived","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L156-L162","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasIsWitnessDerived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasIsWitnessDerived","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L136-L154","doc":"**Source of truth** for the principled atlas:\n  1. confined-particle.md — GB-NF particle registry.\n  2. mass-table-ppb.witness.json — D..⁴⁰Ca. (Dual-column exact symbolic vs Q-CLT proxy trace).\n  3. methodology-deprecation.witness.json — per-particle audit.\n  4. hp_volume.py — ≥ 50-digit Markov-closure → Vol_hyp.\n  5. closed_form_tau_M.py — Active-partition factored exact symbolic trace for $A \\geq 5$.\n  6. hecke_core.py — Q-CLT finite sum approximations tracking active asymptotics.\n  7. y_lambda_wenzl_bridge_extended.py — symbolic-q Wenzl bridge.\n\nUpdates to any input propagate via witness_staleness_tracker.py\nto the rendered appendix on the next `bun run build`.\n\nConcrete predicate: `atomKnotAtlas` is non-empty (the witness\npipeline has produced at least one entry).  After the canonical\nproton and neutron entries above, this is `2 ≥ 1`, provable by\n`decide`.  The genuine \"every entry is witness-derived\" content\nrequires per-entry methodology checks; this minimal predicate\ncatches the regression \"atlas regenerated to empty\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.principledAtlas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.principledAtlas","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L126-L134","doc":"The principled sub-atlas: entries whose methodology is anything\nother than `deprecatedVolumeMatch`.  This is the list cited by\nstatistical summaries and physics claims. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.atomKnotAtlas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.atomKnotAtlas","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L84-L124","doc":"The recursive atom-knot atlas: list of all confined particles and\natoms at q_0 with their Hecke-NF braid words, knot closures, and\nmass predictions.  The `principledAtlas` filter excludes any entry\ntagged `deprecatedVolumeMatch`; statistical summaries cite the\nfiltered list.\n\nConcrete model: contains the canonical proton + neutron entries\nderived from the from-scratch derivation chain; the full atlas\n(D, T, ³He, ⁴He, …) is built by\n`recursive_atom_knot_atlas_render.py` consuming the witness\ninputs enumerated below; consult the rendered markdown on every\nbuild.  The two seed entries here ensure\n`principledAtlas atomKnotAtlas ≠ []`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:recursive-atom-knot-atlas","label":"prop:recursive-atom-knot-atlas","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.methodology","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.methodology","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.err_ppb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.err_ppb","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.err_pct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.err_pct","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.m_AME_MeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.m_AME_MeV","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.m_pred_MeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.m_pred_MeV","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.vol_hyp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.vol_hyp","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.binding_link","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.binding_link","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.rho_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.rho_factor","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.closure_knot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.closure_knot","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.braid_word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.braid_word","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.n_0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.n_0","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.ell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.ell","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.name","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.name","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry.mk","kind":"ctor","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.AtlasEntry","kind":"structure","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L67-L82","doc":"A particle in the atlas at q_0: registry entry from the\nconfined-particle definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.deprecatedVolumeMatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.deprecatedVolumeMatch","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.recursiveOn4He","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.recursiveOn4He","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.magicAFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.magicAFormula","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.manualHistoricalVolumeMatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.manualHistoricalVolumeMatch","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.principledGbNf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.principledGbNf","kind":"ctor","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.principledDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology.principledDerivation","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Methodology","kind":"inductive","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean#L54-L65","doc":"Methodology tag: how the particle-knot identification was obtained.\nOnly `principledDerivation`, `principledGbNf`,\n`manualHistoricalVolumeMatch`, `magicAFormula`, and `recursiveOn4He`\nare admissible in the principled atlas.  `deprecatedVolumeMatch`\nentries are filtered out of the live atlas by `principledAtlas`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}